==Irish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sga|ga|sort=fa}} {{term|fo|lang=sga}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|ga|sort=fa}} {{recons|wo|lang=cel-pro}}, from *''uφo'', from {{etyl|ine-pro|ga|sort=fa}} {{recons|upo|lang=ine-pro}}; compare Greek {{term|ὑπό|tr=hupo|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Middle Welsh {{term|go|lang=wlm}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Ulster}} {{IPA|[fˠæː]|lang=ga}}

===Preposition===
{{ga-prep|sort=fa}}

# {{Ulster|lang=ga|sort=fa}} [[about]], [[concerning]]

====Usage notes====
The standard Irish and Connacht form {{term|faoi|lang=ga}} (Munster {{term|fé|lang=ga}}) means both "under" and "about, concerning". In Ulster, these two meanings are split: {{term|faoi|lang=ga}} means "under", while '''''fá''''' means "about, concerning".

